lemon-chat fix - WebRTC DTLS handshake fails (intermittently) under mbedTLS
==========================================================================

SYMPTOM
  WebRTC audio sometimes fails to connect. ICE reaches connected/completed,
  then DTLS aborts with "DTLS recv: Handshake failed: SSL - An invalid SSL
  record was received" (mbedTLS error -0x7200); the peer goes RTC_FAILED.
  The SAME mbedTLS build connects fine on some paths/servers and fails on
  others - it is intermittent, not a different TLS backend.

ROOT CAUSE
  DtlsTransport::ReadCallback (the mbedTLS receive callback) in
  src/impl/dtlstransport.cpp copies the incoming datagram into mbedTLS's input
  buffer but returns `len` (the size of the buffer mbedTLS offered) instead of
  the number of bytes it actually copied (the real datagram size). So mbedTLS
  believes the datagram is `len` bytes long - the whole offered buffer - rather
  than its true, smaller size, and keeps parsing past the real bytes into the
  uninitialized tail of the buffer, where it reads a bogus record header
  (content type 0) and aborts.

  In the captured failure this broke FRAGMENT reassembly of a ClientHello
  larger than the DTLS MTU: mid-reassembly mbedTLS looked for the next fragment
  inside the same (falsely buffer-sized) datagram instead of the next datagram,
  hit the stale tail, and failed. Whether it triggers depends on the datagram
  sizes / fragmentation (ClientHello size vs the negotiated MTU) and on whatever
  bytes happen to sit past the real datagram - all of which vary with the
  network path. That environment-sensitivity is why the same build works on one
  route (e.g. a remote server) and fails on another (e.g. locally).

  For comparison, the GnuTLS receive callback in the same file returns the real
  byte count (min(buffer, datagram)); the mbedTLS one returned the buffer size.

FIX
  Return the bytes actually copied (`bufMin`) instead of `len`.

APPLY (from repo root, on a clean libdatachannel checkout):
  git apply server-source-code/third-party/libdatachannel-0.24.2/src/impl/dtlstransport.cpp.patch
REVERT:
  git apply -R server-source-code/third-party/libdatachannel-0.24.2/src/impl/dtlstransport.cpp.patch
  (or change `bufMin` back to `len` at the marked line in ReadCallback)

Then rebuild only libdatachannel (it is loaded dynamically):
  cd server-source-code/third-party/libdatachannel-0.24.2 && cmake --build . --target datachannel
  cp libdatachannel.so ../../../buildresult/

==========================================================================
diff --git a/server-source-code/third-party/libdatachannel-0.24.2/src/impl/dtlstransport.cpp b/server-source-code/third-party/libdatachannel-0.24.2/src/impl/dtlstransport.cpp
index a310b04..7619e0a 100644
--- a/server-source-code/third-party/libdatachannel-0.24.2/src/impl/dtlstransport.cpp
+++ b/server-source-code/third-party/libdatachannel-0.24.2/src/impl/dtlstransport.cpp
@@ -661,7 +661,14 @@ int DtlsTransport::ReadCallback(void *ctx, unsigned char *buf, size_t len) {
 
 			auto bufMin = std::min(len, size_t(message->size()));
 			std::memcpy(buf, message->data(), bufMin);
-			return int(len);
+			// FIX (lemon-chat, see dtlstransport.cpp.patch): return the bytes
+			// actually copied (the datagram size), not the buffer size `len`.
+			// Returning `len` told mbedTLS the datagram filled its whole input
+			// buffer, so it parsed past the real data into uninitialized memory
+			// and aborted the DTLS handshake with "invalid record" (record type
+			// 0). The GnuTLS/OpenSSL ReadCallbacks already return the real size.
+			// To revert: change `bufMin` back to `len`.
+			return int(bufMin);
 		}
 
 		// Closed
